        "title": "just pass a hugging face repo id — works with almost any popular model:",
        "summary": "quickstart | configurations | macos | example-python-notebook | faq AirLLM dramatically reduces inference memory usage, letting 70B large language models run on a single 4GB GPU card — without quantization, distillation, or pruning. You can even run 405B Llama 3.1 on 8GB, DeepSeek-V3 671B on ~12GB, and Kimi K3 2.8T — the largest open-source model released to date — on under 4GB, because sparse MoE models stream one expert at a time rather than a whole layer. Updates 2026/07 Kimi K3 2.8T support: the largest open-source model runs on a single card in 3.72GB of VRAM, measured end to end on one RTX 6000 Ada. Per-expert streaming loads only the experts a token actually routes to. K3 brings three",
